Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 05:15:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/15] [GDN] Compute causal_conv1d conv-state offsets in 64
 bits (#658)

The conv-state line pointer is computed as
`conv_states + states_id * conv_states_stride_0` with both operands `int`,
so the product is 32-bit. When conv_state is a view into a larger cache
allocation (as vLLM passes it), stride(0) is the full per-block stride, and
the product passes INT32_MAX at moderate block ids: with a 425,984-element
stride, any block id >= 5042. The kernel then reads and writes a wrong
cache line or faults.

Cast the index to int64_t at all seven sites (causal_conv1d.hpp and the
two XE2 chunk conv1d kernels), as gated_delta_rule already does for the SSM
state offset. Add a test that places a cache line past 2**32 elements.

